      "level": 2,
      "content": "PART A: COMPOSITION OF THE ATMOSPHERE (IN-DEPTH)"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Nitrogen (78%) and Oxygen (21%) together constitute approximately 99% of dry atmospheric gases.",
        "The troposphere contains almost all water vapor and atmospheric dust, making it the zone for all key weather phenomena.",
        "Stratosphere hosts the protective ozone layer, which absorbs harmful ultraviolet radiation from the sun.",
        "Mesosphere is the coldest atmospheric layer, reaching temperatures down to -100°C where incoming meteors burn up.",
        "Atmospheric heating occurs primarily through terrestrial radiation, conduction, convection, and advection."
      ],
      "id": "88jenz0"
    },
