    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Temperature Inversion occurs when warm air overlies cold surface air, halting vertical mixing and trapping pollutants.",
        "Coriolis Force deflects winds to the right in the Northern Hemisphere and to the left in the Southern Hemisphere (Ferrel's Law).",
        "The Ionosphere, part of the Thermosphere, contains charged particles that reflect radio waves back to Earth.",
        "The Equatorial Low Pressure Belt is frequently referred to as the Doldrums due to extremely calm and weak winds."
